CART - Logic

	The Cart module is responsible for managing products that a logged-in user wants to buy later.
	Each cart belongs to one user and is identified using the username extracted from JWT.

	@AuthenticationPrincipal String userId
	because of this one cart per user and no cart without authentication

Cart Data Structure

	Each cart stores 
		userId
		list [obj] of CartItem
		LastUpdate time
	
	CartItem structure
		productCode
		quantity
		name
		priceAtAdd
		imageType
		
	
	Response look like this:
		{
		  "userId": "admin1",
		  "items": [
			{
			  "productCode": "P1001",
			  "quantity": 3,
			  "name": "Samsung S24",
			  "priceAtAdd": 80999,
			  "imageType": "image/jpeg"
			}
		  ],
		  "updatedAt": "2025-01-01"
		}
		
Logic Flow
	URL -> localhost:8080/api/cart/add?Product=P1001&quantity=2
	
	controller send to service
	
	Service method required 3 thing
		userId -> which is userName of user and it will be cartId.
		productCode
		quantity
	
	check quantity >= 0
		false -> InvalidQuantityException
	
	find product by productCode
		True -> continue
		False -> ProductNotFoundException
	
	find userId in cartRepository mean it searching cartId which is userName of user
		True -> continue
		False -> create new Cart Cart Id will be  new userId which is Cart
		
	now once cart created
	we will check if product alredy exist in cartlist
		if exist -> increse it quantity (old quantity + new quantity = new quantity)
		if not -> add new cartItem
	
	update updatedAt
	
	Save Cart
	
	Important part
	One product = one cart item
	Quantity represents how many units the user wants.
	
